00:51:26.513 --> 00:51:31.513
So what is it and what can women do who are experiencing it?

00:51:32.579 --> 00:51:37.143
Reduce the symptomology around it.

00:51:37.143 --> 00:51:39.353
I'm actually really glad to talk about menopause

00:51:39.353 --> 00:51:43.026
because I think it's something that many women feel

00:51:43.026 --> 00:51:44.563
that they can't talk about.

00:51:44.563 --> 00:51:46.033
It's weird, it's like this weird,

00:51:46.033 --> 00:51:48.263
like it happens to every woman, right?

00:51:48.263 --> 00:51:51.043
But it's this sort of not really shameful,

00:51:51.043 --> 00:51:53.493
but like something that, oh, we just don't talk about it.

00:51:53.493 --> 00:51:57.783
Yeah and I try to think about where that comes from.

00:51:57.783 --> 00:52:01.453
I do think that we live in a patriarchal kind of society

00:52:01.453 --> 00:52:05.663
that really values women for the way that they look

00:52:05.663 --> 00:52:09.557
more than the way that they contribute to the world.

00:52:09.557 --> 00:52:12.603
And I think a lot of women feel

00:52:12.603 --> 00:52:15.103
that if they talk about menopause,

00:52:15.103 --> 00:52:19.753
that their significance in the world is diminished somehow,

00:52:19.753 --> 00:52:23.793
that their function to produce children is gone,

00:52:25.653 --> 00:52:27.813
therefore their worth is gone.

00:52:27.813 --> 00:52:30.873
That's something that I've noticed a lot,

00:52:30.873 --> 00:52:31.953
certainly in my patients,

00:52:31.953 --> 00:52:35.343
but also in general society that people feel really

00:52:35.343 --> 00:52:39.692
reluctant to speak up about it and quite low about it.

00:52:39.692 --> 00:52:43.363
Like it's something that, a lot of women feel

00:52:43.363 --> 00:52:45.443
that they've lost something about themselves.

00:52:45.443 --> 00:52:48.303
And I'd really like the conversation to change.

00:52:48.303 --> 00:52:52.783
Because I think that if we can have an empowering idea

00:52:52.783 --> 00:52:54.733
about what menopause can do,

00:52:54.733 --> 00:52:57.853
then it can hopefully help women to actually feel

00:52:57.853 --> 00:53:00.193
that they're even more contributing to the

00:53:00.193 --> 00:53:02.323
world in ways that they couldn't do before.

00:53:02.323 --> 00:53:05.203
There's only very few mammals that have a menopause.

00:53:05.203 --> 00:53:06.955
This is really interesting.

00:53:06.955 --> 00:53:10.673
There's three mammals that experience menopause,

00:53:10.673 --> 00:53:13.083
obviously humans are one of them.

00:53:13.083 --> 00:53:15.365
Do you have any idea what the other ones could be?

00:53:15.365 --> 00:53:18.603
Well, I would think it would be chimpanzees or apes.

00:53:18.603 --> 00:53:19.953
You'd think so.

00:53:19.953 --> 00:53:21.453
But actually it's not.

00:53:21.453 --> 00:53:23.311
Don't tell me it's dolphins.

00:53:23.311 --> 00:53:25.283
Nearly, (laughs)

00:53:25.283 --> 00:53:26.116
Whales.

00:53:26.116 --> 00:53:28.493
It's yeah.
It's Orcas and pilot whales.

00:53:28.493 --> 00:53:29.453
Wow.

00:53:29.453 --> 00:53:31.280
Orcas, pilot, whales, and humans with the.

00:53:31.280 --> 00:53:32.653
That's so bizarre.

00:53:32.653 --> 00:53:34.956
I would've just presume that every mammal,

00:53:35.793 --> 00:53:38.733
every female mammal experiences that.

00:53:38.733 --> 00:53:40.963
No, and this is significant

00:53:40.963 --> 00:53:43.313
because what it tells us I believe

00:53:43.313 --> 00:53:46.429
is that we have a very specific purpose

00:53:46.429 --> 00:53:48.872
past our reproductive years.

00:53:48.872 --> 00:53:52.854
We have a very specific survival advantage in having

00:53:52.854 --> 00:53:56.136
a menopause, whereas every other mammal does not.

00:53:56.136 --> 00:53:59.303
And there's actually something called the grandmother

00:53:59.303 --> 00:54:03.363
hypothesis, which essentially tries to explore this.

00:54:03.363 --> 00:54:05.333
And the idea is that

00:54:05.333 --> 00:54:08.063
the reason that humans have menopause is

00:54:08.063 --> 00:54:12.733
because women in society have such value

00:54:12.733 --> 00:54:16.133
in making sure that we continue as a species.

00:54:16.133 --> 00:54:17.893
And we maybe look after younger children,

00:54:17.893 --> 00:54:19.283
we would bring families together.

00:54:19.283 --> 00:54:21.693
We would bring communities together.

00:54:21.693 --> 00:54:24.663
There's a very strong survival advantage to having women

00:54:24.663 --> 00:54:26.823
exist past their reproductive years.

00:54:26.823 --> 00:54:29.113
And I think that should be celebrated

00:54:29.113 --> 00:54:31.563
cause it's something very special, so yeah.

00:54:31.563 --> 00:54:35.474
Yeah, the idea that evolution has prioritized this

00:54:35.474 --> 00:54:37.883
because when the village expands

00:54:37.883 --> 00:54:40.865
and there's more women around to care-take for

00:54:40.865 --> 00:54:44.443
the many young ones, then everybody benefits as a result.

00:54:44.443 --> 00:54:47.113
Everybody benefits and there's a survival advantage.

00:54:47.113 --> 00:54:49.043
Think that would be the case with chimpanzees

00:54:49.043 --> 00:54:52.383
and apes and all other manner of mammals as well.

00:54:52.383 --> 00:54:53.585
Yeah, you'd think so.

00:54:53.585 --> 00:54:55.273
But it's interesting because when you look at pilot whales

00:54:55.273 --> 00:54:57.923
and orcas, they have a very matriarchal society,

00:54:57.923 --> 00:55:00.723
don't they, they go around in matriarchal pods

00:55:00.723 --> 00:55:03.043
and it's the grandmother that makes sure that

00:55:03.043 --> 00:55:06.363
the mother and the babies are all together and protected.

00:55:06.363 --> 00:55:07.391
So.

00:55:07.391 --> 00:55:08.393
Right so we're off the rails here

00:55:08.393 --> 00:55:09.963
being a patriarchal society.

00:55:09.963 --> 00:55:13.533
Right, we are we're evolutionarily meant to be

00:55:13.533 --> 00:55:15.184
a matriarchal society.

00:55:15.184 --> 00:55:16.663
Okay.

00:55:16.663 --> 00:55:17.496
I think so.

00:55:17.496 --> 00:55:19.733
That's my hypothesis. (laughs)

00:55:19.733 --> 00:55:21.553
Yeah, interesting.

00:55:21.553 --> 00:55:26.553
So this occurs in every woman at a certain age

00:55:28.324 --> 00:55:31.243
and the symptoms range and severity.

00:55:31.243 --> 00:55:33.383
They do, and that's another interesting thing is the

00:55:33.383 --> 00:55:36.583
symptoms can range in severity based on

00:55:36.583 --> 00:55:40.303
where the woman lives in some to some degree.

00:55:40.303 --> 00:55:44.803
So I mentioned Japanese women and vasomotor flashes.

00:55:44.803 --> 00:55:47.743
That's one of the main symptoms for women certainly

00:55:47.743 --> 00:55:51.432
in the US and the UK is hot flashes or flashes.

00:55:51.432 --> 00:55:52.673
Whereas interestingly,

00:55:52.673 --> 00:55:55.205
Japanese women don't tend to experience that.

00:55:55.205 --> 00:55:58.533
There was some anthropology work done

00:55:58.533 --> 00:56:01.483
in sort of two provinces of India

00:56:01.483 --> 00:56:03.203
that showed that menopause brought about

00:56:03.203 --> 00:56:05.593
increased quality of life in those women

00:56:05.593 --> 00:56:08.843
because they were able to achieve more status.

00:56:08.843 --> 00:56:11.443
They were able to spend more time with men.

00:56:11.443 --> 00:56:16.273
They had more of a say in the household over the

00:56:16.273 --> 00:56:19.653
sort of the sons and the wives and other younger children.

00:56:19.653 --> 00:56:21.113
So in actual fact,

00:56:21.113 --> 00:56:24.323
when they were sort of questionnaires to those women,

00:56:24.323 --> 00:56:25.793
they had an increased quality of life

00:56:25.793 --> 00:56:28.943
and far less menopausal symptoms than-

00:56:28.943 --> 00:56:31.223
But what is the, I'm trying to understand

00:56:31.223 --> 00:56:34.853
what that's attributable to the increase in quality of life?

00:56:34.853 --> 00:56:38.703
I think that a lot of the symptoms of menopause

00:56:38.703 --> 00:56:43.703
can be dreadful, but also that the society in which we live,

00:56:44.533 --> 00:56:47.803
if it's more supportive to women going through menopause,

00:56:47.803 --> 00:56:52.653
can dramatically reduce the effect on our lives.

00:56:52.653 --> 00:56:56.593
So when you have a society that is supportive

00:56:56.593 --> 00:56:58.993
or where the women is considered to be

00:56:58.993 --> 00:57:02.153
a value, wise, contributing,

00:57:02.153 --> 00:57:05.064
then it can be actually quite empowering

00:57:05.064 --> 00:57:07.213
and it can hopefully potentially

00:57:07.213 --> 00:57:09.663
lead to less in the way of symptoms.

00:57:09.663 --> 00:57:12.428
That's not to say that it's all psychological.

00:57:12.428 --> 00:57:15.283
No, there's some very physical and very real problems,

00:57:15.283 --> 00:57:19.030
but I think it's important to just be aware that in society

00:57:19.030 --> 00:57:22.573
and the way that we view women is really important

00:57:22.573 --> 00:57:25.203
because it can affect our long term happiness.

00:57:25.203 --> 00:57:26.273
It can affect the way that we feel

00:57:26.273 --> 00:57:27.813
we can contribute to the world.

00:57:27.813 --> 00:57:29.953
And that can also affect the symptoms that we experience

00:57:29.953 --> 00:57:32.323
much with any kind of medical or health condition.

00:57:32.323 --> 00:57:33.696
That's fascinating.
Yeah.

00:57:33.696 --> 00:57:35.795
With the social environment and a supportive social

00:57:35.795 --> 00:57:39.212
environment can have that kind of impact.

00:57:40.162 --> 00:57:41.389
And it's-

00:57:41.389 --> 00:57:42.673
Or it seems to appear that that's the case.

00:57:42.673 --> 00:57:43.983
It seems to appear that way.

00:57:43.983 --> 00:57:45.573
And it's true for all sorts of things.

00:57:45.573 --> 00:57:48.353
There was a really interesting study that showed

00:57:48.353 --> 00:57:52.556
that people who had increased happiness scores,

00:57:53.713 --> 00:57:56.133
positivity, a good sense of humor.

00:57:56.133 --> 00:57:58.193
Their longevity was increased even

00:57:58.193 --> 00:58:00.343
when they were living with chronic disease.

00:58:00.343 --> 00:58:04.303
So I think the importance of a supportive community

00:58:04.303 --> 00:58:07.013
shouldn't be underestimated, which is why opening up

00:58:07.013 --> 00:58:08.463
this kind of conversation is really

00:58:08.463 --> 00:58:11.353
important so that men and women can understand how

00:58:11.353 --> 00:58:14.593
to support the third of women that are right now,

00:58:14.593 --> 00:58:17.347
peri or postmenopausal it's huge.

00:58:17.347 --> 00:58:18.347
Sure.

