01:50:13.493 --> 01:50:18.493
guidance to kick people into this kind of lifestyle.

01:50:18.533 --> 01:50:20.963
Like when somebody comes to you and they're ready to go,

01:50:20.963 --> 01:50:24.970
like what kind of words of wisdom can you provide

01:50:24.970 --> 01:50:28.331
to empower them to embark upon this journey

01:50:28.331 --> 01:50:30.353
with confidence and perhaps a few

01:50:30.353 --> 01:50:33.403
practical things that they could do to make it work

01:50:33.403 --> 01:50:35.793
within the construct of their busy life?

01:50:35.793 --> 01:50:37.233
Well, I think the number one thing

01:50:37.233 --> 01:50:40.583
is think of simple swaps that you enjoy,

01:50:40.583 --> 01:50:41.993
which we've already touched on.

01:50:41.993 --> 01:50:43.543
Number two would be again,

01:50:43.543 --> 01:50:45.833
to think about the values that are important to you.

01:50:45.833 --> 01:50:48.473
And if you could try and live by those each day,

01:50:48.473 --> 01:50:50.533
it really helps you with the food choices you're making,

01:50:50.533 --> 01:50:52.653
as well as everything else.

01:50:52.653 --> 01:50:54.993
Maybe just three, just three values.

01:50:54.993 --> 01:50:57.143
That would be really helpful.

01:50:57.143 --> 01:50:59.633
I dunno if you have any sort of top three

01:50:59.633 --> 01:51:01.273
that you have in your head right now?

01:51:01.273 --> 01:51:02.913
Well, I was just thinking if I was you

01:51:02.913 --> 01:51:04.343
and I was seeing patients

01:51:04.343 --> 01:51:07.423
and I knew that they could come back and make another

01:51:07.423 --> 01:51:09.651
appointment and follow up, I would try to,

01:51:09.651 --> 01:51:11.383
because I'm competitive,

01:51:11.383 --> 01:51:13.093
I would try to find a way to gamify it.

01:51:13.093 --> 01:51:15.773
I'd see like, well, here's your numbers in these categories.

01:51:15.773 --> 01:51:18.713
I wanna see them go down 10% in each.

01:51:18.713 --> 01:51:21.043
So I want you to come back in 30 days

01:51:21.043 --> 01:51:23.663
and we're gonna do it again, so it start,

01:51:23.663 --> 01:51:25.283
it's almost like goal oriented.

01:51:25.283 --> 01:51:26.645
Yeah it's very practical.

01:51:26.645 --> 01:51:29.133
Here's what we're driving towards.

01:51:29.133 --> 01:51:30.793
And if you can come back

01:51:30.793 --> 01:51:33.393
every 30 days or every 60 days or something like that,

01:51:33.393 --> 01:51:35.646
and we can evaluate the progress,

01:51:36.677 --> 01:51:39.263
that creates a level of accountability and engagement.

01:51:39.263 --> 01:51:41.643
Yeah, I do that at work. I definitely do.

01:51:41.643 --> 01:51:43.903
And it's quite nice because you've got actual numbers

01:51:43.903 --> 01:51:48.383
to work with and you have a goal for people to have in mind.

01:51:48.383 --> 01:51:50.863
I think making those goals specific

01:51:50.863 --> 01:51:53.423
and time orientated really helps.

01:51:53.423 --> 01:51:56.333
So I mean, generally for people at home,

01:51:56.333 --> 01:51:58.343
if you want to do that for yourselves,

01:51:58.343 --> 01:52:00.553
then maybe you could get your blood test done,

01:52:00.553 --> 01:52:02.583
your blood work done, and then decide, okay,

01:52:02.583 --> 01:52:05.103
in the course of four or eight weeks,

01:52:05.103 --> 01:52:06.693
I'm gonna get to this number

01:52:06.693 --> 01:52:08.653
and this is how I'm gonna do it.

01:52:08.653 --> 01:52:09.893
But certainly my practice,

01:52:09.893 --> 01:52:11.753
I found that with my patients

01:52:11.753 --> 01:52:13.503
getting average blood sugar readings,

01:52:13.503 --> 01:52:16.268
getting cholesterol or lipid panel profile

01:52:16.268 --> 01:52:17.579
or blood pressure readings actually,

01:52:17.579 --> 01:52:20.563
they can change over time as well with nutrition.

01:52:20.563 --> 01:52:23.453
It's quite nice to then be able to have that accountability,

01:52:23.453 --> 01:52:26.453
to be able to bring them back and to encourage them as well.

01:52:27.380 --> 01:52:29.803
I think for some of my patients then gamifying,

01:52:29.803 --> 01:52:30.943
it is good, but for others,

01:52:30.943 --> 01:52:33.063
they just tend to need that little bit of extra

01:52:33.063 --> 01:52:34.920
like compassion and care and

01:52:34.920 --> 01:52:37.883
make sure that they know that I'm gonna be there

01:52:37.883 --> 01:52:39.793
and I'm gonna check it again when they come back.

01:52:39.793 --> 01:52:41.663
So yeah, it's a good strategy.

01:52:41.663 --> 01:52:44.623
I also think being specific,

01:52:44.623 --> 01:52:47.323
it's fine to say it's okay to do this gradually,

01:52:47.323 --> 01:52:50.113
but how are you specifically going to accomplish that?

01:52:50.113 --> 01:52:51.323
Because to just say, well,

01:52:51.323 --> 01:52:53.823
I'm just gonna try and I'm gonna start eating more plants

01:52:53.823 --> 01:52:56.423
seems very vague, but if you say, listen,

01:52:56.423 --> 01:52:58.643
I know you love cream in your coffee.

01:52:58.643 --> 01:52:59.933
So for the next 30 days,

01:52:59.933 --> 01:53:03.793
you're gonna do almond milk or soy milk or whatever it is.

01:53:03.793 --> 01:53:05.673
And you're just gonna master that one thing.

01:53:05.673 --> 01:53:08.873
Like that's all you have to do is like that one thing.

01:53:08.873 --> 01:53:11.903
And it makes it very doable because,

01:53:11.903 --> 01:53:14.369
and it's kind of like a go, no go thing.

01:53:14.369 --> 01:53:16.753
Right you can wrap your head around it.

01:53:16.753 --> 01:53:18.233
This is what I'm doing.

01:53:18.233 --> 01:53:20.943
And then after 30, 60 days of that,

01:53:20.943 --> 01:53:22.213
it's like, okay, well, that's just,

01:53:22.213 --> 01:53:23.673
I don't even think about that anymore.

01:53:23.673 --> 01:53:25.273
What's the next thing that I can do?

01:53:25.273 --> 01:53:26.283
Yeah exactly.

01:53:26.283 --> 01:53:28.553
And I think that makes it more like,

01:53:28.553 --> 01:53:30.973
'cause the human brain is weird, right.

01:53:30.973 --> 01:53:31.806
And if you're just like,

01:53:31.806 --> 01:53:33.013
well I'm just gonna eat more plants.

01:53:33.013 --> 01:53:34.503
Like what does that mean, right.

01:53:34.503 --> 01:53:38.583
And I think that will wan in terms of how people are

01:53:38.583 --> 01:53:42.363
kind of consciously engaging with each meal and each food

01:53:42.363 --> 01:53:44.093
choice that they're making throughout the day.

01:53:44.093 --> 01:53:44.926
Yeah, you're right.

01:53:44.926 --> 01:53:47.283
And it's also so individual to people as well.

01:53:47.283 --> 01:53:49.403
So I could have one person sitting in front of me

01:53:49.403 --> 01:53:50.273
who thinks, okay,

01:53:50.273 --> 01:53:53.343
well I can start with my milk and I'll have someone else

01:53:53.343 --> 01:53:54.703
sitting in front of me that thinks, okay,

01:53:54.703 --> 01:53:57.273
well I know I can just start with my breakfasts and I'll

01:53:57.273 --> 01:53:59.173
have someone else sitting in front of me that thinks, okay,

01:53:59.173 --> 01:54:01.613
well I know I can just start with two tablespoons

01:54:01.613 --> 01:54:03.643
of milled flaxseed a day.

01:54:03.643 --> 01:54:06.583
And then, so it really depends on the person,

01:54:06.583 --> 01:54:08.793
what route I go down.

01:54:08.793 --> 01:54:10.766
Based on what they feel they can achieve based on what they

01:54:10.766 --> 01:54:12.876
already are doing, which is, yeah.

01:54:12.876 --> 01:54:14.873
It's quite good to individualize it in that way

01:54:14.873 --> 01:54:17.013
and make it really super specific.

01:54:17.013 --> 01:54:19.913
I also think people future trip,

01:54:19.913 --> 01:54:21.973
I'm sure they say to you, I can't do it

01:54:21.973 --> 01:54:24.233
'cause I have to go to a wedding this summer,

01:54:24.233 --> 01:54:25.766
in four months or something like that.

01:54:25.766 --> 01:54:27.483
It's like, that doesn't matter.

01:54:27.483 --> 01:54:28.903
Like this is a sober thing, it's like,

01:54:28.903 --> 01:54:29.873
what are you doing today?

01:54:29.873 --> 01:54:31.933
Can your head hit the pillow sober tonight?

01:54:31.933 --> 01:54:33.393
That's all you have to worry about.

01:54:33.393 --> 01:54:35.493
What is your next food choice when you, okay,

01:54:35.493 --> 01:54:37.073
you're gonna go to the grocery store today?

01:54:37.073 --> 01:54:38.243
Like what are you gonna buy?

01:54:38.243 --> 01:54:41.383
Like just focusing on making that next right choice

01:54:41.383 --> 01:54:43.173
and not worrying about what you're gonna do tomorrow.

01:54:43.173 --> 01:54:45.463
Obviously with food, there is some planning involved,

01:54:45.463 --> 01:54:47.533
like you're getting food for the next day

01:54:47.533 --> 01:54:48.693
or for the following week.

01:54:48.693 --> 01:54:51.953
But to the extent that you can just be rooted in the moment

01:54:51.953 --> 01:54:55.593
and not freak out about like the rest of your life or,

01:54:55.593 --> 01:54:58.568
oh my God, I'm never gonna have this food ever again.

01:54:58.568 --> 01:54:59.685
That's so true.

01:54:59.685 --> 01:55:01.379
'Cause I think that really works

01:55:01.379 --> 01:55:02.593
at cross purposes with the goal.

01:55:02.593 --> 01:55:05.237
It's so true. That is so true.

01:55:05.237 --> 01:55:08.413
And I think about that in other aspects of life as well,

01:55:08.413 --> 01:55:11.833
you can generally manage to do something just for today.

01:55:11.833 --> 01:55:16.253
You know you can manage to make the right kind

01:55:16.253 --> 01:55:18.793
of choice for your health and body just for today.

01:55:18.793 --> 01:55:21.923
Or you can choose not to feel angry just for today

01:55:21.923 --> 01:55:23.473
or you can choose not to worry

01:55:23.473 --> 01:55:25.616
about something just for today.

01:55:27.753 --> 01:55:29.113
And this is a slight tangent,

01:55:29.113 --> 01:55:32.813
but I actually have this daily mantra that I do,

01:55:32.813 --> 01:55:35.323
which is exactly that.

01:55:35.323 --> 01:55:39.533
It's in Japanese and in English it means

01:55:39.533 --> 01:55:44.533
just for today, do not be angry, do be worried, be grateful,

01:55:44.943 --> 01:55:48.586
do your duties fully, and be kind to all living things.

01:55:49.423 --> 01:55:52.003
And that is the mantra that I actually repeat to myself

01:55:52.003 --> 01:55:54.323
twice a day, every day in Japanese.

01:55:54.323 --> 01:55:55.723
And it's just for today.

01:55:55.723 --> 01:55:58.503
Well, you know what I'm gonna say right now.

01:55:58.503 --> 01:56:00.323
I'm gonna make you do it in Japanese.

01:56:00.323 --> 01:56:01.313
Okay.

01:56:01.313 --> 01:56:02.193
Oh gosh, okay.

01:56:02.193 --> 01:56:03.093
The pressure's on.

01:56:04.308 --> 01:56:08.225
(speaking in foreign language)

01:56:14.127 --> 01:56:15.793
That's beautiful.

01:56:15.793 --> 01:56:17.613
I think that's a good place to end it.

01:56:17.613 --> 01:56:21.193
I can't imagine a better ending than with that mantra.

01:56:21.193 --> 01:56:23.214
It's called the gokai.

01:56:23.214 --> 01:56:25.153
The gokai, where did you find that?

01:56:25.153 --> 01:56:27.723
It's part of my Jekiden and Reiki practice,

01:56:27.723 --> 01:56:29.123
which is a whole other topic.

01:56:29.123 --> 01:56:31.540
That's a whole other, yeah, that's a whole there,

01:56:31.540 --> 01:56:33.045
I know a little bit about that,

01:56:33.045 --> 01:56:34.473
but that's a whole other podcast.

01:56:34.473 --> 01:56:35.623
Next time.

01:56:35.623 --> 01:56:36.473
Next time.

01:56:36.473 --> 01:56:38.599
But yeah.
Next house call.

01:56:38.599 --> 01:56:41.003
It's a great way of living, being, thinking.

01:56:41.003 --> 01:56:43.013
You don't have to put pressure on yourself

01:56:43.013 --> 01:56:45.203
to be your best self every day.

01:56:45.203 --> 01:56:46.456
Just try and do it today.

